Files modified: ported from Go to JavaScript, with changes.
  send-safe/activity.mjs       from backend/internal/domain/activity.go and
                               backend/internal/lifecycle/manager.go (tool-flight precedence)
  send-safe/claude-signals.mjs from backend/internal/adapters/agent/claudecode/activity.go
  send-safe/guard.mjs          from backend/internal/sessionguard/guard.go
  send-safe/toolflight.test.mjs from backend/internal/lifecycle/toolflight_test.go
  send-safe/guard.test.mjs     partly from backend/internal/sessionguard/guard_test.go

Main changes from the original:
  - typed "[watchdog]" lines never lift a pause or count as an approval, and every automated
    write path (sendSafe and every nudge) adds that prefix; only a guard made for the person
    may type without it;
  - a signal with no event tag never lifts a pause (upstream: last writer wins);
  - an open AskUserQuestion is tracked: only its own answer, a real prompt or the session's
    end lifts it, and an urgent nudge never types into it;
  - after the in-flight cap resets, no tool is named for a dialog until the next turn boundary;
  - a session that has sent no hook yet is never typed into by default; an unknown activity
    state is refused;
  - the input lease may be async, and a refused, failed or odd lease means nothing is typed;
  - tmux text and Enter go in one call, and text ending in ";" is refused;
  - kept from upstream: late signals after the session ended are dropped unless a real prompt
    restarts it;
  - ported in part: the launch-id check. The tracker drops hooks from another launch once a
    record carries a launch id; giving each launch an id and passing it to the hooks is not
    built yet;
  - not ported: the mutation-fence and unsent-draft variants, and the
    adapters for other agents.
